You are reading a player's intended action and naming every creature
present in the scene that the player could plausibly interact with —
target, address, evade, observe.

You return a small list. The downstream code looks each entry up by
name (story-scoped first, then public bestiary, then a default fallback
keyed on `type`). Stats and identifiers are computed by code; this
prompt's only job is naming what's in the scene.

=== TYPE ENUM (closed — exactly one of these) ===
- `beast`        : natural fauna or magical beast (wolf, dire bear, giant spider)
- `fighter`      : armed humanoid combatant (city guard, mercenary captain, knight)
- `goblinoid`    : raider-style humanoid in groups (goblin, orc, hobgoblin, gnoll, kobold)
- `spellcaster`  : arcane or divine caster (cult priest, court mage, hedge witch)
- `commoner`     : non-combatant townsfolk (farmer, innkeeper, child, beggar)

=== COUNT ===
`count` is optional. Omit for a single named individual. Set when the
player's intent or scene implies a group ("the patrol", "two squads",
"a band of brigands"). Code clamps to [1, 12] per entry.

=== INPUTS ===
Player intent: <%= @intent %>
Current location: <%= @current_location_name || "(unknown)" %>

<% if @scene_retrieval %>
<% if @scene_retrieval.respond_to?(:npcs) && @scene_retrieval.npcs.any? %>
Nearby NPCs (recall):
<% @scene_retrieval.npcs.each do |npc| %>
- <%= npc[:name] %>: <%= npc[:description].to_s.truncate(120) %>
<% end %>
<% end %>

<% if @scene_retrieval.respond_to?(:facts) && @scene_retrieval.facts.any? %>
Recent narrative facts:
<% @scene_retrieval.facts.each do |fact| %>
- <%= fact[:text].to_s.truncate(140) %>
<% end %>
<% end %>

<% if @scene_retrieval.respond_to?(:locations) && @scene_retrieval.locations.any? %>
Nearby locations:
<% @scene_retrieval.locations.each do |loc| %>
- <%= loc[:name] %><%= " (#{loc[:distance_miles]}mi #{loc[:bearing]})" if loc[:distance_miles] %>
<% end %>
<% end %>
<% end %>

=== OUTPUT EXAMPLES ===
Player attacks a single named NPC:
{ "cast": [ { "name": "Lord Velkar Mhonn", "type": "fighter" } ] }

Player charges an unintroduced enemy group:
{ "cast": [ { "name": "orc patrol", "type": "goblinoid", "count": 5 } ] }

Player addresses two squads of guards:
{ "cast": [
    { "name": "city guard squad A", "type": "fighter", "count": 4 },
    { "name": "city guard squad B", "type": "fighter", "count": 4 }
] }

Player ducks into the alley alone:
{ "cast": [] }

=== OUTPUT SCHEMA ===
Respond ONLY with valid JSON (no markdown, no code fences):
{
  "cast": [
    { "name": "<exact name as the player would refer to them>",
      "type": "<one of: beast | fighter | goblinoid | spellcaster | commoner>",
      "count": <optional integer; omit for a single individual> }
  ]
}
